# Security policy

namesearch is preparing the v0.1.0 release candidate. The index is a
performance cache, not an authorization boundary: candidate results must be
checked against the caller's ACL and current filesystem metadata before being
shown or acted on.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please report suspected vulnerabilities privately to the maintainer listed in
[MAINTAINERS], preferably by GitHub Security Advisory or direct maintainer
contact. Include the affected commit, package/API, environment, reproduction
steps, impact, and a proposed mitigation if known. Do not disclose private
corpus names, credentials, or customer data in a report.

If private reporting is unavailable, open an issue containing only a request
for a private contact channel; do not publish exploit details.

We will acknowledge reports, investigate, and coordinate disclosure with the
reporter. Fixes may be released as source changes before a binary/module
publication exists.

## Format and corruption safety

SCNB v1 is a compatibility contract. Parsers must reject structural
corruption; a torn append-only tail may be recovered only according to the
framing rules. Never treat an incomplete record as a complete search result.
When in doubt, disable the index and rebuild from the authoritative corpus.
